## 22. End-to-end generation flow

Actual intended complete flow:

1. User opens app at `/`.
2. User signs up or logs in through Firebase.
3. AuthProvider records current user.
4. PrivateRoute allows access to `/dashboard` or `/generate`.
5. Dashboard defaults to Studio tab.
6. User selects:
   - model,
   - platform,
   - content type,
   - topic,
   - tone,
   - creativity,
   - font size,
   - prompt.
7. PromptInputArea helps user craft prompt with chips and readiness/character UI.
8. GeneratePost gets Firebase ID token.
9. GeneratePost sends authenticated request to backend.
10. Backend validates body with Joi.
11. Backend verifies token with Firebase Admin.
12. Backend optionally expands very short prompts using OpenRouter.
13. Backend checks in-memory cache.
14. Backend builds platform/tone/content-type-specific system prompt.
15. Backend calls Ollama `/api/chat` for one or more variants.
16. Backend retries transient failures.
17. Backend cleans AI output.
18. If Ollama produces nothing, backend attempts Hugging Face fallback.
19. Backend computes strategy brief: hashtags, framework, tip, best time, char count, max chars, engagement score.
20. Backend caches and returns JSON.
21. Frontend displays result in PostResultView.
22. User can copy, download markdown, regenerate, browse variants, submit feedback.
23. Frontend logs generation to Firestore.
24. Zustand usage stats update analytics.
25. History tab listens to Firestore and shows the saved result.

